this is a really interesting piece uh in  the new york in the los  angeles times rather by doyle mcmanus  called  joe biden has become the anti-reagan  and his speech to congress will make  that clear now this was of course  written before  last night's speech but it was really  confirmed by the address joe biden gave  to a joint session of congress last  night  joe biden and his biden amics his  economic ideas as they're being called  are truly based on the opposite  principles of reaganomics reaganomics  boiled down was  supply side economics sometimes called  trickle-down  the belief that cutting government  spending is good for the economy cutting  taxes  income taxes and capital gains taxes  particularly on the rich is good for the  economy  reducing regulation on business is good  for the economy tightening the money  supply is good for the economy  and also reaganomics includes the idea  that giving  people help will make them lazy joe  biden  and bidenomics as they've been dubbed  are the  exact opposite of reaganomics now to be  really clear  this doesn't have to mean that biden is  ultra left or is left as bernie or  whatever  but his views are truly the opposite of  reaganomics reaganomics is supply side  economics  joe biden is demand side stimulate the  economy with spending and by increasing  demand reaganomics is about cutting  government spending they almost think  you can cut your way to prosperity  joe biden believes you increase  government spending on the right things  and that's good for the economy it  creates jobs it injects money  into small business reaganomics is  cutting income taxes and capital gains  especially for the rich but biodynamics  is about increasing them on the people  most able to pay  since we know that the hoarding of money  by those people  is not economically stimulative compared  to well thought out properly targeted  government programs  reaganomics wants to reduce regulation  on business and let it rip  let them do whatever the hell they want  joe biden recognizes we must regulate  in order to prevent the further  destruction of our environment which  long term  would be terrible for the world and of  course terrible for the american economy  reaganomics wants to cut the money  supply often they want higher federal  funds rates  biodynamics is about increasing the  money supply  through thoughtful stimulus spending  while reaganomics would have you believe  that if you give people help it makes  them lazy  the biden idea is that if you give  people help  you make it so that they're not  constantly treading water trying to  avoid drowning  they will become more innovative they  will be more predisposed to become more  productive members of society  notice that nothing about the biden view  is remotely socialist it's almost really  just keynesianism it's a different  form of capitalism some people don't  like that  some people didn't like the fdr new deal  because they were well to the left  socialists wouldn't really have liked  the new deal because it did a lot  to sort of cement industry in american  uh the american economy  it's similar with biden there's nothing  socialist about this and as doyle  mcmanus writes in the la times piece  reagan made people hate government and  then debate  whether government should do anything at  all because the default is government is  bad  joe biden's approach is government doing  things can be popular  if they are done correctly if they are  the right things to begin with  vaccine distribution coveted stimulus  are two great starting points because  they're so popular even with many  republicans  that could then build goodwill towards  the proposals  like what joe biden outlined at last  night's speech  this is very different than what we saw  after reagan which was the demonization  of government  the constant drum beat about cut  programs cut social programs  and we could be entering a new era now i  don't say that hyperbolically it's just  you know there are errors eventually  errors change  we could be shifting to government being  seen as a tool  to help people if the tool is used  correctly even republicans we have to  admit under trump  sort of drifted away from as much  demonization of government you still saw  it of course  but they've drifted away from it a  little bit and part of it is that while  the republican party is busy fighting  this culture war  they've completely abandoned whoa sorry  i punched my mic they've completely  abandoned  policy if the options are government  doing stuff under biden  or nothing happens either way while  republicans just talk about the culture  war in dr  seuss government doing things starts to  look  quite good and that's part of why we see  a strong support among republicans  comparatively for uh joe biden on  vaccination  as well as joe biden's 1.9 trillion  dollar coveted stimulus so we are going  to follow this very closely but  the antithesis of reaganomics appears to  be  what joe biden is rolling out as  economic policy
 

